<table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Befallen</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=100">Mellifleur</a> - 7/25/2001 6:55:35 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">9</font><br>
			1st floor at 9 solo....you can pretty much single pull...<br><br>2nd Floor at 12 - 15 ....some nasty trains can happen here so be vewy vewy cawefwul wen hunting your wabbits here...<br><br>3rd floor = 16 - 25 . Some easy Mobs...some Hard...but the drops are not worth the risk of being here at this level.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Beholders Maze</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=100">Mellifleur</a> - 7/25/2001 6:58:24 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">15</font><br>
			At 15 you can get a sow and invis and run to the Runnyeye entrance and single pull Minotaurs and Muddites there...Best suited for Melee classes.<br><br>16-23 Run around the zone and bust up Muddite elders, some Minors will still con blue and Chasm Minotaurs will give you a run for your money in these levels.<br><br>Wait until at Least 34 to try the Evil eye Lords.<br>No Joke !<br>i tried Lord Soptyvr at 26.....He smacked me around like a kid in a supermarket.<br>
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Butcherblock Mountains</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=89">Llewelyn</a> - 7/11/2001 6:13:52 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">8</font><br>
			What seems to a little known but excellent hunting are is the Druid Circle in the south west of the zone.  There a four dwarf skeletons that spawn around it, though far enough from each other that they don't all agro, offering constant fighting and ok loot.  Hand the bone chips into Kaladim Paladins guild for xp, faction and more loot, and sell other loot to the druid vendor at the ring for reasonable prices.  Once you are killing skeles faster than their spawn rate, head over and kill the three at the obelisk just to the east as well.  Fantastic for soloing, hardly ever camped.  Stay here till level 10.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Frontier Mountains</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=51">Mikuras</a> - 6/8/2001 9:21:15 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">27</font><br>
			Go to the Giants Fort here. Most MOBs will con either Blue or Yellow to you at 28. Watch out for the craigs though. They're mean! Last night each time we pulled one, we pulled to. All I can say is make sure you have sow and know how to get to the zone. I'd say this is really good experience once you hit your first hell level. But I'd leave after level 32 or so.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Greater Faydark</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=64">Konst</a> - 6/21/2001 7:47:12 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">5</font><br>
			Group and kill Orc's. They give out good XP for lower levels, and collect as many CrushBone belts from their dead corpses as you can. These can be traded into a NPC in Kaladim for Experience points and Equipment you can sell for money. Once you reach level 9, head out to Butch Block.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Highhold Pass</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=19">Jammer</a> - 6/8/2001 6:12:48 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">13</font><br>
			Strap on your fighting gear, beg a SoW from your nearest druid. Run through Kithicor Forrest to High Hold Pass, and Start Camping the Gnolls. When you Hit lvl 15 head on over and Camp the Orcs til about lvl 19. Lots of GReat Fun, it will hone your group skills, and there is some pretty decent loot. Oh and dont forget to get a bind. You can bind anywhere in Zone as long as you can bind or find someone willing to do so.<br><br>-Jammer
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - 6/8/2001 10:46:08 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">15</font><br>
			As Jammer mentioned you can bind anywhere in zone but you can also head into the Keep (if your not KOS to the Guards) and there is a bank handy. You can pretty much live here through those levels aside from getting new spells or training.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Lake of Ill Omen</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - 6/7/2001 4:06:32 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">18</font><br>
			Start this zone around 18 or 19.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Lower Guk</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=100">Mellifleur</a> - 7/25/2001 7:05:33 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">35</font><br>
			The EQ Gods have blessed you my child.<br><br>at 35 go in..make a right then left down a ramp...then right ( better have IVU ) ...to a river...jump into the river and swim right...you will pop out in whats called the Bedroom. Good xp here 33 to 38....3 Undead ghouls spawn here + 2 more and a bat in the adjecent room...<br><br>38 + ...i suggest getting in a Arch Mage , or a Frenzy Group...from 38 and on...you will spill your milk on how fast the xp shoots through with a good group constantly pulling. and the Loot is 4 pp per drop and a chance at a SMR ( 2.5 k )...or a FBSS ( the holy item )....how to get there you ask ?....from bedroom go through left tunnel..then make left into another tunnel.....remember..have IvU. !!!<br><br>you'll come out on a bridge. Jump off the left side and there is a hallway there. This is " safe Hall "...no mobs here. then walk through safe hall and make first right by slave cages. the a left...right...left....youll be in a room with green drapes....walk through the drapes to find a secret wall....then make a right...left...and right....this is the Frenzy pulling area.<br><br>If i confused you...ask me in Game...chances are i will be in Lower Guk trying for the FBSS.....=o)
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Nagafens Lair</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=45">Thundor</a> - 7/8/2001 10:37:55 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">35</font><br>
			This zone is great for exp and loot from 35 to <br>50+
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=100">Mellifleur</a> - 7/25/2001 6:52:28 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">40</font><br>
			I have to disagree with Thundore on his posting on Nagafens Lair at 35......i was in Naggys Lair at 44 and 45 and i seen 35's and such come into this zone and get bent over and used as a bad blind date. The kobolds are good....if you can grab a single one from the trains that run by. This place is Rated #2 in Train listing on Everlore.com....# 1 was Karnors castle.....at 35 - 50 i suggest you do Lower Guk....get a IvU and pick a spot you want to camp...get in a group and watch your xp bar race by....35 = Bedroom....40 = everything but Lord.....45 + = Ghoul Lord his and compadres....not to mention the Loot here makes Nagefens Lair look like Nektolous Forest...in Naggy you can get a green silk drape - PC = 400....in Lower Guk...you can get a SMR - PC = 2.5 k...you do the math.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Northern Desert of Ro</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=82">Crazyincali</a> - 6/12/2001 4:07:26 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">8</font><br>
			This zone is great exp. when hunting in group, stay away from red mummies, unless you are a cleric and have ward undead and a tank . :) Madman are bad news to also note that if you run to a guard for help, he will not kill the Madman i think its because hes a human, so if you see a madman run to zone... :) hehehe
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Rathe Mountains</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=21">Giant</a> - 6/8/2001 5:48:15 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">29</font><br>
			While you can hunt here at real early levs if you come through Ferrott, this zone comes into <br>itself in your 30ish range.  In just 2 hours last night I cleared about 90pp killing HGs! <br>It's absolutely essential that your in a well balanced group though.  Our group was 2 tanks,<br>1 wiz, 1 dru, 1 shammy(me) and 1 ench.  And we still died once when trained by another <br>group.  On key seems to have the ench or cleric if u got 1 to Fear the giant, although make<br>sure they're snared, damn things can outrun SoW when Feared.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Southern Karana</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - 6/8/2001 2:04:40 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">24</font><br>
			At lvl 24 you can group at the gnoll spires by the entrance to split paw. There is an exp bonus to this zone and the spawn rate of the gnolls is pretty fast. Besides the static spawns there are 'runners', usually 2 at a time.<br><br>The gnolls are usually yellow or red at this level and in a small 3 or 4 person group the exp is great. With the right group you can rely on a bard for healing in a 3 person group, and downtime matches the spawn rate.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=56">MachinShin</a> - 6/9/2001 10:32:32 AM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">27</font><br>
			killing gnolls till lvl 30
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>Splitpaw Lair</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - 7/9/2001 1:28:58 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">30</font><br>
			This zone has a 13% exp bonus.<br><br>Instead of camping the slow spawns of the spires in SK head on into the lair and camp 'the lounge' just a little ways from the entrance.<br><br>Get a full group with good crowd control and the exp will fly by. Head in early when your in the late 20's and you'll level fast. Loot is very good as well. Fine Steel weapons on every other corpse and up to 4pp in cash. Run up to NK to sell and kill those willowisps to trade at the gypsies for 9pp for the book.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

			<tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#800000"><font color="White"><b>West Commonlands</b></font></td></tr>

		<tr><td align="left">
			<ul type="circle"><li>
			<a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - 6/7/2001 4:46:14 PM<br>
			Best for level: <font color="#7E92D7">10</font><br>
			Start camping those Dervs until lvl 14 or so.
			</li></ul>
		</td></tr>

</table>
	</td>
